{
	title: 'Web transcript that reads like the demo',
	description: `The web transcript has the improvements the old Hal tried in its Solid demo (artifact demo.tsx, tags [F1]..[F16]) and never shipped:
- Stable rows [F1, F8]: the item list is keyed by position (<For keyed={false}>). Items only append, except an edit of the last prompt cutting the tail, so a row keeps its DOM and local state (open or closed) when a snapshot replaces every item object or a streaming item gains fields.
- Cards [F11, F12]: every item is a card coloured like the terminal (prompt, assistant text, thinking, tool call with its result, command output, turn end). Thinking and tool cards collapse, closed by default. A click anywhere on a card toggles it, except on links and a click that ends a text selection; the header is a real <button> with aria-expanded, hidden contents are inert. Opening and closing animate the height (CSS grid 0fr to 1fr); closing is faster.
- Bottom follow [F4-F7]: a reader within 50 px of the bottom stays at the same distance from it as content grows (new items, streamed text, a card opening); one scrolled further up is left alone. Measure before the change.
- Smooth follow [F10]: a new item fades in while the view glides (strong ease-out, about 200 ms, fade about 300 ms) to the new bottom; streamed lines jump; wheel, touch or scroll keys cancel a glide; prefers-reduced-motion jumps.
- Sending [F15] glides to the very bottom even when scrolled far up, and trackpad momentum does not cancel that glide.
- Composer [F13, F14]: one bottom panel holds a status line like the terminal's (idle, thinking, writing, running <tool>, paused, reconnecting; a pulsing dot while busy; aria-live polite), the textarea (grows with its content up to 40% of the height) with a Send button disabled while empty, and a line of key hints. Enter sends, Shift+Enter is a newline, nothing sends during IME composition.
- Hal's cursor [F16]: a line after the last item holds a blinking block cursor in the assistant colour, dimmed while thinking streams; the textarea keeps its native caret.
- One scroller: the transcript scrolls and nothing inside it does; long tool output and code wrap.
Not in scope: ID links, deep links and the target outline [F2, F3, F9] need short block ids that hal2 items do not have yet; the demo's debug controls (slow motion, step key, offline toggle).
Test the scroll maths (gap, whether to follow, glide target) and the status line as pure functions. Check the rest in a real browser at phone and desktop widths and say in the commit what you checked.`,
	status: 'planned',
	needs: [
		'1b'
	],
	notes: [
		'demo.tsx is self-contained and runs as is under Solid 2; its comments explain each decision, including the failures behind them (why keyed-by-id rows closed and flashed; why only scroll keys cancel a glide; why the send glide is `forced`). Its CSS uses hand-picked hex colours: take the layout and motion, but colours come from colors.ts (task 1w).',
		'keepBottom() calls flush() before measuring because Solid 2 applies DOM updates in a microtask.',
		"old-scroll.ts and old-viewport.ts are the old client's near-bottom check and mobile keyboard handling (visualViewport); reference only. old-frontend-design.md is the design guidance the old Hal used for UI work."
	]
}
